The keystones are the twenty cut gems set out by the host of the [[Phenomena/Pilgrimage|pilgrimage]] at [[Geography/Calaria/Ragged Roost|Ragged Roost]] as the price of a place aboard his strider. The one he showed from the scaffolding is a faceted cerulean stone floating in an embossed golden box; the other nineteen were placed in or around [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]]. A keystone buys passage for its bearer and one vehicle with whatever it will carry, and two keystones buy two vehicles. The only rule is that the bearer hold a keystone in his hands when the strider leaves, six months after the night of the announcement; the host cares nothing for how it was come by or who found it. Guests learn more about the stones by trading at the party or by taking on the games along the street.

Keystone 14 belonged to a [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]] calling itself [[Org/Prime Meridian/Rapid Connection|Rapid Connection]], a collector of paintings in oil or acrylic on canvas. The Party holds it now, having traded the Heart the [[People/Kellum Quinn|Kellum Quinn]] *Second Meaning* for the stone and for the waiver of all Prime Meridian fees. Every rival who hunted it is dead: [[People/Sbrtlby Jotes|Sbrtlby Jotes]] and his hired henchmen, and [[Org/Concordia/People/Crawford Reeves|Crawford Reeves]] and [[Org/Concordia/People/Louis Maller|Louis Maller]] of [[Org/Concordia/index|Concordia]].

The Party keeps keystone 14 in a lead-lined safe set in cement under the floor of the room the [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anouk Marchal|Marchal]] twins share at the [[Sin and Tonic]]. Lead or running water will block a simple locating spell, but neither stops a caster who names the stone itself.

The holder of keystone 15 would trade it for a relic of the [[Org/Iridescent Church/index|Iridescent Church]], a reliquary or a holy book. Second-Among-Equals [[People/Thistle Monroe|Thistle Monroe]] is the one most likely to knowingly lead to it.

With a week to go, the host spoke through the Party's keystone. He said the nineteen stones placed around the city are now locked away in one place or another, and that the departure is at 9am exactly one week later, from the same place the gathering first set out from. The Party means to be aboard, believing the pilgrimage is bound for wherever the singer of the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]] is. They have confirmed some of the other keystone-holders but do not have the full list.
